# For Dockerfile.derived, whose build context is this directory. An allow-list, not a deny-list: deployers copy this
# file beside their own dist-pack/, into a directory that may also hold a .env, .git/, keys or other sources, and
# whatever this file does not exclude is sent to the builder (a remote builder uploads it). So everything is excluded,
# then only dist-pack/ (build-pack's output, which the image installs with npm ci --omit=dev) and the Dockerfile are
# let back in. A node_modules inside dist-pack/ is excluded again: the pack stage installs its own on Linux.
*
!dist-pack/
!Dockerfile.derived
dist-pack/node_modules
